  "family": "skeletonChain",
  "description": "The op-stream chain over OPAQUE payloads (Phase 549), under the canonical profile (the {seq, actor, op} pre-image, the empty genesis) and SHA-256: hash = sha256(prevHash + \"|\" + payload), lower-case hex. Every op is a string the chain splices into its pre-image unread, so a host certifies the chain with no op codec; an actor is its canonical text. An `append` vector chains `input.entries` from `input.anchor` and expects each record's seq, prevHash, payload (the pre-image, exactly) and hash, and the tip the next record hangs from. A `walk` vector walks `input.records` from `input.anchor` (sequence, then prev-link, then hash, first fault reported) and expects `intact` with the tip, or `break` with the index in the run, the reason's canonical spelling, and the expected and got values. Every expectation is computed by calling Core (ChainShape.append, ChainShape.walk, ChainShape.tip); there is no kitVersion stamp.",
